Fixed. The Progress dashboard no longer uses a scroll view, the time range buttons are back below the chart, and the chart height is capped dynamically so the whole dashboard fits on the current screen.

Verified: `npm --prefix apps/mobile run typecheck` passes.

Committed as `405efcd Fit progress dashboard without scrolling`.

::git-stage{cwd="/Users/walden/Documents/Orca9"}
::git-commit{cwd="/Users/walden/Documents/Orca9"}

Fixed the actual cause: the chart was still capped at the old max height, so the added bottom margin had nowhere visible to go. I lowered the Progress chart height cap so the range buttons should now visibly sit above the tab bar.

Verified with `npm --prefix apps/mobile run typecheck`.

Committed as `f407491 Make progress range spacing visible`.

::git-stage{cwd="/Users/walden/Documents/Orca9"}
::git-commit{cwd="/Users/walden/Documents/Orca9"}

Good screenshot. I changed the range row itself to render 12px higher, instead of relying on bottom padding that the tab bar was covering/clipping.

Verified with `npm --prefix apps/mobile run typecheck`.

Committed as `9acedae Offset progress range controls from tab bar`.

::git-stage{cwd="/Users/walden/Documents/Orca9"}
::git-commit{cwd="/Users/walden/Documents/Orca9"}

I replaced the “visual nudge” with an actual layout change: the chart now has a lower max height and the range row has real bottom margin, so the buttons should sit visibly above the tab bar instead of being clipped at the separator.

Verified with `npm --prefix apps/mobile run typecheck`.

Committed as `ac867b3 Shorten progress chart for range spacing`.

::git-stage{cwd="/Users/walden/Documents/Orca9"}
::git-commit{cwd="/Users/walden/Documents/Orca9"}

I changed the approach: the range buttons are now absolutely pinned `18px` above the bottom of the Progress scene, instead of depending on bottom padding/margins that were getting clipped. I also reserved bottom space and trimmed the chart height budget so the chart should stay clear of them.

Verified with `npm --prefix apps/mobile run typecheck`.

Committed as `acd17b9 Pin progress range controls above tab bar`.

::git-stage{cwd="/Users/walden/Documents/Orca9"}
::git-commit{cwd="/Users/walden/Documents/Orca9"}

Yep, the fixed pin solved the tab-bar collision but created that big dead zone. I removed the absolute pinning and restored the range buttons to normal flow under the chart, keeping only a small bottom cushion. The chart stays shorter, so it should still avoid hugging the tab bar.

Verified with `npm --prefix apps/mobile run typecheck`.

Committed as `c07646e Tighten progress range control spacing`.

::git-stage{cwd="/Users/walden/Documents/Orca9"}
::git-commit{cwd="/Users/walden/Documents/Orca9"}

I think your diagnosis was right. The chart was too short to naturally push the range buttons down, so changing the bottom margin wasn’t enough.

I changed the range row to use `marginTop: "auto"` and kept `marginBottom: 5`, so the leftover vertical space goes above the buttons and they should sit about 5px above the tab bar.

Verified with `npm --prefix apps/mobile run typecheck`.

Committed as `73f53c7 Anchor progress range controls with auto spacing`.

